# 162 · Research and knowledge bugs found by the v0.1.1 audit: error pages as sources, domain counts, cut text in the knowledge base

**Status:** `VERIFIED` · **Version:** [v0.1.1](../../roadmap.md#v011) · **Depends on:** [160](160-v010-audit.goal)

## What

The harness and knowledge reviewers of the v0.1.1 audit (goal [160](160-v010-audit.goal)) found these bugs in research runs and in the knowledge base. Each fix comes with a regression test that fails without it.

1. **Error pages become sources.** No code checks the HTTP status of a fetch (`src/harness/research/fetcher.ts` `request` and `get`; `src/harness/research/research.ts` `fetch`). A 403 challenge page, a 404, a 429 or a 503 is archived as a source, and a claim that quotes it passes the verbatim check. A URL whose first fetch got a 429 or 503 is then "already archived" for the rest of the run. The fix: refuse a non-2xx answer before it is archived; 404 and 410 are lasting refusals, 429 and 5xx refusals that can pass. The campaign modes page states the rule.
2. **Answer cards count hosts, not registrable domains.** `claimFor` in `src/harness/research/cards.ts` counts `source.domain`. The review package, the report and the teachers' reads count registrable domains since 94ebe1b; the cards came later the same day and missed it.
3. **The knowledge base cuts agent text.** `src/core/kb-index.ts:398` and `:440` strip old `Result:`, `Dropped:` and `Verdict:` lines with unanchored patterns. An experiment whose details contain `Result: ` loses everything after it when its result arrives; an attempt whose hypothesis contains `Verdict: ` loses its hypothesis. Later runs, From past research and every export's `knowledge.jsonl` read the cut text. The ledger keeps the words, so the record is whole and the projection is wrong. The fix keeps an item's state in structured fields, not in lines of prose, and rebuilds the items once from control's events.
4. **A queue edit never reaches the knowledge base.** `experiment_edited` is not in `KB_EVENT_KINDS` (`src/core/kb-index.ts`). An edited experiment keeps its first words there, and From past research seeds new runs with them.
5. **Control and the harness read old event names differently.** `src/control/kb.ts` (`catchUp`, `readAgain`) does not read the kinds renamed on 2026-10-15, where `src/harness/kb-part.ts` does. `indexEvent` reads them, for every caller.
6. **Two documents can share one file in `knowledge/`.** `part()` and `itemPath()` in `src/harness/knowledge.ts` map `lane-1/a-b.md` and `lane-1/a/b.md` to one file, and cut names at 100 characters; the second overwrites the first. A short hash of the full reference keeps them apart.
7. **A briefing can lose an item without a word.** `byOrigin` (`src/control/kb.ts:625-632`) finds nothing when two rigs used the same run name in one campaign, and the item is left out of the briefing.
8. **The final report reaches the knowledge base cut.** The report's event keeps its first 60,000 characters with no cut note (`src/harness/research/research.ts:1528`), and the item its first 20,000. The paper comes first, so the answer cards and the panel's decisions after it are lost to later runs. A cut is always said, and the paper, each answer card and the review panel's decisions become items of their own, as the owner decided.
9. **A message to `all` can wait for lanes that never run.** `readersOf` (`src/harness/messages.ts`) takes the last lane count, where the scheduler puts the owner's first. With the owner's 2 lanes and a teacher's 4, the message's receipts never complete. One `lanesAtWork` in `src/harness/agents/coordinator.ts` for both.

## Why

Experiment integrity: a claim counts only when its quotes are in the archived text of a source, and an error page is not one. The knowledge base is what later runs read, so its items must say what the record says. CONVENTIONS.md: "Every bug that is found gets a regression test".

## Done when

- [x] Each of the nine bugs is fixed, with a regression test that fails without the fix.
- [x] Control's knowledge items written before the fix of item 3 are rebuilt, and the rebuild is tested.
- [x] The campaign modes page and the knowledge base reference say what changed.
- [x] The fast checks pass, and the steering acceptance check.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-26, owner (the [guide](../../code-clean-up-guide.md#7-the-owners-questions)'s question 23): the paper, each answer card and the review panel's decisions become knowledge-base items of their own.
- 2026-10-26, owner: v0.1.1 breaks compatibility with v0.1.0 ([decisions](../../decisions.md#releases-and-planning)). Where goal 125 has already removed the old event names, an item here that reads them is done by that removal.

## Open questions

- The number rule's exemptions: a paper may restate a number from the run's own questions and hypotheses, while a card or a reviewer's answer may not (`src/harness/research/paper.ts:476-489`, `cards.ts:287`, `review.ts:770`). No reason was found for the difference. One set for all three?
- The submission limit for a hypothesis or a claim: 2,000 characters (what the clients cut to) or 4,000 (what the server takes)?

## Progress

- 2026-10-26: Goal written from the v0.1.1 audit's harness and knowledge reports.
- 2026-10-27 06:06 UTC: Started by goal 172, step 2. Item 1 fixed: the fetcher refuses an answer that is not a 2xx before anything is archived (`statusRefusal` in `src/harness/research/fetcher.ts`): a 404, a 410 or another 4xx for good, a 408, a 429 or a 5xx as a failure that can pass (`tests/harness/research/fetch-status.test.ts`, which fails without the fix). The campaign modes page states the rule.
- 2026-10-27 06:08 UTC: Item 2 fixed: an answer card's claims count registrable domains, as the review package, the report and the docs do (`claimFor` in `src/harness/research/cards.ts`; `tests/harness/research/cards.test.ts`, where two hosts of one owner are one domain).
- 2026-10-27 06:22 UTC: Items 3 and 4 fixed: the knowledge index keeps an experiment's result and an attempt's verdict in fields, and writes them after the agents' words, never reading them back from the text; an `experiment_edited` reaches the experiment's item, which keeps its result (`src/core/kb-index.ts`; `tests/core/kb-index.test.ts`). Control's knowledge base reads its experiments' and attempts' events once more (reading 3), so items cut by the earlier reading are whole again (`tests/control/kb.test.ts`). The targets give the index an item's fields (`item` in place of `body`). The knowledge base reference says what changed. The tables of control's knowledge base moved to `src/control/kb/schema.ts`.
- 2026-10-27 06:25 UTC: Item 5 fixed: `indexEvent` reads events recorded under their names from before 2026-10-15 for every caller, and control's one-time reading again selects them too (`tests/control/kb.test.ts`, which fails without the fix). The harness's export no longer maps them itself.
- 2026-10-27 06:27 UTC: Item 6 fixed: each file of past research in `knowledge/` ends with a short hash of its rig, run and ref, so two items whose cleaned or cut names match get files of their own (`itemPath` in `src/harness/knowledge.ts`; `tests/supervisor/kb-sync.test.ts`). The tests take file names from `itemPath` (`tests/helpers/kb-file.ts`). The knowledge base reference gives the new names.
- 2026-10-27 06:32 UTC: Item 7 fixed: a briefing item's origin carries its rig (`from.rig`, which control always gives), and control finds the item by it, so of two rigs' runs of one name the right item comes; an item left out is logged with which and why (`briefingFromKb`, moved to `src/control/briefing.ts`; `tests/control/briefing.test.ts`). The copy of a past experiment finds its result by its rig too. The signed commands, MCP tools and knowledge base references and two how-to pages follow.
- 2026-10-27 06:36 UTC: Item 8 fixed: a cut is always said (`cutSaid` in `src/core/kb-index.ts`), in the final report's event (60,000 characters) and in every report, paper and card item (20,000); the paper, each answer card and each decision of the review panel are items of their own, of the kind `report` (refs `paper`, `card-q<index>`, `decision-<kind>-<key>`), as the owner decided; control's one-time reading again reads them for earlier runs (`tests/core/kb-index.test.ts`). The knowledge base reference lists the new items and the cut.
- 2026-10-27 06:40 UTC: Item 9 fixed: one `lanesAtWork` in `src/harness/agents/coordinator.ts` counts the lanes at work for the scheduler and for a message's readers, the owner's lane count before an advisor's, so a message to everyone never waits for a lane that never runs (`tests/harness/messages.test.ts`, which fails without the fix). All nine items are fixed; the steering acceptance check is still to run.
- 2026-10-27 06:59 UTC: Verified. The full fast checks passed on e33b4436, after its nine items, and the steering acceptance check passed on 16030a14. Moved to `_completed/`.

